Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage
• "country_code": filter to U.S. publications only ( 'US' )  
• "kind_code": identify granted publications ( 'B2' )  
• "grant_date": numeric YYYYMMDD value to restrict 2008‑01‑01 – 2018‑12‑31  
• "publication_number": unique document identifier; returned in results / counted  
• "claims_localized": VARIANT array that stores each claim in plain text; must be flattened to inspect the text  
• "claims_localized_html": same information in HTML; can be used for a cross‑check  
• "family_id": optional grouping if you want to avoid counting several publications of the same simple family  

Typical conditions you will need  
1. "country_code" = 'US'  
2. "kind_code" = 'B2'  
3. "grant_date" BETWEEN 20080101 AND 20181231  
4. ( flattened_claim_text ILIKE '%claim%' )  or NOT ILIKE '%claim%' depending on the step  

Ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries
(Each query is limited to 20 rows for inspection; all identifiers are quoted)

```sql
-- 1. Quick look at US B2 grants and their grant dates
SELECT "publication_number",
       "grant_date",
       "kind_code"
FROM "PATENTS"."PATENTS"."PUBLICATIONS"
WHERE "country_code" = 'US'
  AND "kind_code"   = 'B2'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Add the time window 2008‑2018
SELECT "publication_number",
       "grant_date"
FROM "PATENTS"."PATENTS"."PUBLICATIONS"
WHERE "country_code" = 'US'
  AND "kind_code"   = 'B2'
  AND "grant_date" BETWEEN 20080101 AND 20181231
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Preview the raw JSON structure in "claims_localized"
SELECT "publication_number",
       "claims_localized"
FROM "PATENTS"."PATENTS"."PUBLICATIONS"
WHERE "country_code" = 'US'
  AND "kind_code"   = 'B2'
  AND "grant_date" BETWEEN 20080101 AND 20181231
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Flatten one element from "claims_localized" to check its keys
SELECT "publication_number",
       f.value
FROM "PATENTS"."PATENTS"."PUBLICATIONS" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."claims_localized") f
WHERE t."country_code" = 'US'
  AND t."kind_code"   = 'B2'
  AND t."grant_date" BETWEEN 20080101 AND 20181231
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Extract the plain text of each claim (assuming key name "text")
SELECT "publication_number",
       f.value:"language"::STRING          AS "lang",
       f.value:"text"::STRING              AS "claim_text"
FROM "PATENTS"."PATENTS"."PUBLICATIONS" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."claims_localized") f
WHERE t."country_code" = 'US'
  AND t."kind_code"   = 'B2'
  AND t."grant_date" BETWEEN 20080101 AND 20181231
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Show claims that DO contain the word 'claim' (case‑insensitive)
SELECT DISTINCT t."publication_number"
FROM "PATENTS"."PATENTS"."PUBLICATIONS" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."claims_localized") f
WHERE t."country_code" = 'US'
  AND t."kind_code"   = 'B2'
  AND t."grant_date" BETWEEN 20080101 AND 20181231
  AND f.value:"text"::STRING ILIKE '%claim%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Show claims that do NOT contain the word 'claim'
SELECT DISTINCT t."publication_number"
FROM "PATENTS"."PATENTS"."PUBLICATIONS" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."claims_localized") f
WHERE t."country_code" = 'US'
  AND t."kind_code"   = 'B2'
  AND t."grant_date" BETWEEN 20080101 AND 20181231
  AND f.value:"text"::STRING NOT ILIKE '%claim%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Count (per publication) how many of its individual claims lack the word 'claim'
SELECT t."publication_number",
       COUNT(*) AS "num_claims_without_claim_word"
FROM "PATENTS"."PATENTS"."PUBLICATIONS" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."claims_localized") f
WHERE t."country_code" = 'US'
  AND t."kind_code"   = 'B2'
  AND t."grant_date" BETWEEN 20080101 AND 20181231
  AND f.value:"text"::STRING NOT ILIKE '%claim%'
GROUP BY t."publication_number"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Cross‑check using the HTML version of the claims
SELECT DISTINCT t."publication_number"
FROM "PATENTS"."PATENTS"."PUBLICATIONS" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."claims_localized_html") f
WHERE t."country_code" = 'US'
  AND t."kind_code"   = 'B2'
  AND t."grant_date" BETWEEN 20080101 AND 20181231
  AND f.value:"text"::STRING NOT ILIKE '%claim%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final count of unique US‑B2 patents granted 2008‑2018 whose claims lack the word 'claim'
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT t."publication_number") AS "patent_count_no_claim_word"
FROM "PATENTS"."PATENTS"."PUBLICATIONS" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."claims_localized") f
WHERE t."country_code" = 'US'
  AND t."kind_code"   = 'B2'
  AND t."grant_date" BETWEEN 20080101 AND 20181231
  AND f.value:"text"::STRING NOT ILIKE '%claim%';
```

